Usage:
  rhythm-soundcheck snapshot <url> --eaa
  rhythm-soundcheck run <url> --modules +keyboard

The keyboard module walks each page the way a keyboard user would, in Chrome
only. It presses Tab until focus comes back to the start (up to
keyboard.max_tabs), then Shift+Tab back, and records every stop. On the
first page of each URL group and on keyboard.pages it opens and closes
menus, dialogs and disclosures by keyboard and checks where focus goes. Key
flows (flows with keyboard: true or send) run at --level flows;
rhythm-soundcheck flows init --keyboard writes four to edit.

Checks:
  keyboard/trap (error, wcag 2.1.2): Keyboard focus is trapped.
  keyboard/not-reachable (warning, wcag 2.1.1): Clickable element can't be
      reached by keyboard.
  keyboard/not-operable (warning, wcag 2.1.1): Control doesn't respond to
      Enter or Space.
  keyboard/menu (warning, wcag 2.1.1): Submenu doesn't open by keyboard.
  keyboard/focus-lost (warning, wcag 2.4.3): Focus is lost after closing.
  keyboard/dialog-focus (warning, wcag 2.4.3): Dialog doesn't take or keep
      focus.
  keyboard/no-focus-ring (warning, wcag 2.4.7): No visible focus indicator.
  keyboard/focus-invisible (warning, wcag 2.4.7): Focused element is hidden.
  keyboard/context-change (warning, wcag 3.2.1): Moving focus changes the
      page.
  keyboard/skip-link-broken (warning, wcag 2.4.1): Skip link doesn't move
      focus to the content.
  keyboard/skip-link-missing (notice, advisory): No skip link before a long
      run of stops.
  keyboard/escape (notice, advisory): Escape doesn't close it.
  keyboard/focus-obscured (notice, wcag 2.4.11 with --wcag 2.2): Focused
      element is covered by fixed content.
  keyboard/flow (error, wcag 2.1.1): Key flow can't be finished by keyboard.
  keyboard/error-not-linked (warning, wcag 3.3.1): Form errors aren't tied
      to their fields.

Settings (keyboard: in .soundcheck/config.yaml):
  - max_tabs: Tab presses per page before the walk stops, 10-2000 (default
    150); a walk that stops there is capped, never a trap.
  - widgets: menus, dialogs and disclosures tested per page, 0-200 (default
    10).
  - trap_after: presses on the same element or region that count as a trap,
    3-20 (default 4).
  - skip_link: expected (a missing skip link is a notice), required (a
    warning) or off.
  - pages: globs of the pages whose widgets are tested besides the first of
    each URL group.
  - ignore: CSS selectors the walk steps over, such as a cookie banner.

What the walk never does:
  - press Enter on a link that leaves the page, or Enter or Space on a
    submit control or anything that looks destructive (delete, remove, log
    out, unsubscribe, place order, pay, buy, checkout, empty cart);
  - type into fields, act inside frames from other sites or on
    keyboard.ignore selectors;
  - run on /wp-admin or /wp-login.php.

A key flow with keyboard: true holds every request that would send data: the
step that would send counts as done and the rest are listed as not run.
keyboard: send really submits, only on this machine or a private address or
with --staging. It never submits on a site listed under production.
